ck('05-place-fields.md',78,94,'The small-band tangent argument derives slope weighting rather than presenting an unexplained named formula. The density is joint height/slope density at a random position; its weighting removes the excess contribution of shallow crossings.','Supplement S9-S13; author notes Kac–Rice and expected-crossing sections')
ck('05-place-fields.md',96,124,'The constructed curve, independence proof, two Gaussian densities and u substitution jointly establish the exact crossing density. Neither high thresholds nor global independence are needed for this mean.','Supplement S10-S13; direct integration; fig:PLACE-CROSSINGS inspected')
ck('05-place-fields.md',126,134,'The finite interval identity counts the active left edge once. Its convention is stated before the expected count, and removing clipped fields is explicitly a different convention.','Mainali2025 Eq8; direct component-counting identity')
ck('05-place-fields.md',138,166,'The occupied and inactive fractions divided by event density yield stationary field and gap means. The text guards against an invalid finite-sample ratio argument and gives explicit inversion. This is enough without introducing Palm probability vocabulary.','Supplement S14-S15; direct algebra')
ck('05-place-fields.md',168,168,'Recalculation gives Q=.1356660609, nu=.0362126851/m, means3.74636845m and23.86826429m, and finite-track expected count7.37820309. Displayed values are correctly rounded and labeled model calculations.','Fig4A q=1.1,sigma=2.4; independent Python arithmetic')
ck('05-place-fields.md',170,170,'The high-threshold Poisson and exponential approximations are conditional on decaying distant correlations. The periodic-process counterexample and within-field crossing dependence prevent an unsupported implication from stationarity.','Supplement S3 high-threshold discussion; direct scope check')
ck('05-place-fields.md',172,181,'Zero-truncation is derived by conditioning a Poisson law, with the omitted zero term explained. At lambda1, excluded fraction36.7879% and conditional mean1.5819767 agree. Its use in the 2D fit is source-supported.','Mainali2025 Eq5 and parameter inference in2D; earlier Poisson teaching 01-foundations.md lines39-88')
ck('05b-place-sizes.md',3,20,'The opening asks for a distribution beyond its mean and clearly separates approximate high-excursion geometry from the exact boundary-slope law. The reconstruction states smoothness, isotropy, nondegeneracy, high-q and component sampling assumptions before use.','Supplement S4; guide derivation scope')
ck('05b-place-sizes.md',22,35,'Hessian and coordinate delta are defined, Gaussian conditioning is derived from an independent remainder, and conditional curvature fluctuations are distinguished from selecting actual maxima. This supplies the reason large peaks become relatively round.','Supplement S22; direct covariance differentiation and Gaussian regression')
ck('05b-place-sizes.md',37,63,'The parabola gives radius sqrt(2 epsilon/q) sigma. Peak-count ratios give scaled excess U=q epsilon with exponential survival. The higher-dimensional polynomial factor is explained and linked forward as a check, rather than relied on without any justification. The text explicitly stops short of a convergence theorem.','Supplement S22-S25, algebra checked; later05c Euler leading count')
ck('05b-place-sizes.md',65,80,'The full width constant includes sqrt2 and yields beta=q²/(8sigma²). Peak rate is quadratic in linear size in the limit. Finite exponents1.42/1.46 and1.75/1.71 match Fig3C-D, and cube-root volume is kept distinct from volume.','Mainali2025 Fig3C-D inspected; S22-S23 checked in PDF; Fig4C and5A-C')
ck('05b-place-sizes.md',84,116,'The unit-ball conversion, gamma definition, variable change and Jacobian yield p_d(s). Every dimension uses size in distance^d, while beta has inverse-distance² units. The high-threshold scale is explicitly not an exact finite-threshold identity.','Mainali2025 Eq1; supplement S18; direct integration and geometry; fig:PLACE-SIZE-GEOMETRY inspected')
ck('05b-place-sizes.md',118,155,'The mean and higher moments follow from u=beta s^(2/d), with normalization shown. The density table has the correct powers in1D/2D/3D. The dimensionless w scale and nonlinear U transform are distinguished; a divergent density is not an atom at zero.','Eq1; direct gamma integrals; tbl:PLACE-SIZE-LAWS and fig:PLACE-SIZE-DENSITY-COLLAPSE inspected')
ck('05b-place-sizes.md',157,159,'For q5,sigma1 the means are.50132565,.25132741,.12599688 in their respective dimensions. The exact-crossing mean comparison gives45.9816% atq1.1 and3.73008% atq5, matching rounding. These examples show the practical size of the approximation error.','Independent Python arithmetic from displayed formulas')
ck('05b-place-sizes.md',161,171,'The supplement correction note is justified: S18 multiplies by mean size, S23 lacks sqrt2, and S25 has a positive quadratic sign. All were checked on original PDF pages13-15, printed12-14. The guide appropriately makes no claim about author code using those mistakes.','Original mainali-2025-supplement.pdf PDF13-15; direct parabola and moment algebra')
ck('05b-place-sizes.md',175,188,'Gaussian restriction explains the dimension of slice predictions. The explicit difference between selecting a field and sampling spatial lines prevents a false chord-distribution argument. Sphere-alternative volumes and peak rates were matched by construction, while slices and EC disagree, exactly as S2 states.','Mainali2025 Fig2/main text; supplement FigS2A-C')
ck('05b-place-sizes.md',192,216,'Slope-weighted crossing selection gives a Rayleigh density with no q dependence. The factor a is retained for rate slopes. The independent high-q width check uses the exact slope law with approximate local curvature, not an exact width claim. Finite differences at.1m are labeled measurements with limited resolution.','Mainali2025 Fig3E and boundary-slopes Methods; author notes slope-at-upcrossing; direct Jacobian')
ck('05c-place-tests.md',3,29,'The opening motivates topology beyond sizes and counts. Components, holes, tunnels and cavities are explained with correct disk/ring/shell examples before Betti terminology. The constructed plot has1-2=-1,1-1=0,4 and3 and nested active sets.','Mainali2025 Euler Methods; direct elementary topology; fig:PLACE-TOPOLOGY inspected')
ck('05c-place-tests.md',31,51,'Morse and multidimensional Kac–Rice are explicitly invoked mathematical results, with the unproved theorem scope stated. Critical point, gradient density and determinant volume factor explain what is being counted. Signed densities are not passed off as positive counts.','Taylor2006 Theorem4.1, section5.1/Eq5.1 and piecewise-smooth-domain remark; Mainali2025 Eq8-10')
ck('05c-place-tests.md',53,83,'The conditional Hessian determinant calculation is sound: Gaussian odd products vanish, each off-diagonal/diagonal pair leaves-lambda², giving b,b²-1,b³-3b. The integrals yield1,q,q²-1 factors with phi(q). The derivative check of -q phi(q) is correct.','Direct determinant expansion; Taylor2006 Gaussian EC densities')
ck('05c-place-tests.md',85,105,'Face counts2^(d-j) choose(d,j), independent normal-gradient sign factors and face sizes give the correct box boundary terms. General-domain limits are explicit. A cube at L/sigma10,q0 gives EC=-20.05565, correctly rounded; q->+-infinity limits hold.','Mainali2025 Eqs8-10; direct face combinatorics and Python arithmetic')
ck('05c-place-tests.md',107,117,'Identification of EC with count is restricted to rare simple blobs. Volume dominance and leading-q approximation are separately named. Occupied-volume/count recovers the limiting mean independently. The gain fit before EC comparison and observable threshold range are retained.','Supplement S16-S17; Mainali2025 EC Methods and Fig3F-H')
ck('05c-place-tests.md',121,135,'The table correctly distinguishes fitting summaries by environment. Main text supplies20-cell slice sample despite displaced STAR cross-references; source Fig5D gives40 short-tunnel cells. Lognormal comparison uses centered moments; in-sample likelihood/BIC/AIC and simulation error bars are not represented as held-out prediction or full uncertainty.','Mainali2025 parameter-inference Methods, Fig1/2/5D; main text printed1114; Eqs5-7')
ck('05c-place-tests.md',137,147,'The.5Hz rectification,3D median filter and10cm bins, large-volume removal, boundary exclusion for peaks and1Hz width cutoff match Methods. S1/S5 cutoff sensitivity and S2 curvature measurements are accurately described without promising exact reconstruction of a whole surface.','Mainali2025 processing/peak/rate-width Methods; supplement S1,S2,S5')
ck('05c-place-tests.md',149,151,'Environment trends are limited to the observed small set, and the unexplained3D sigma4.0 conversion is not labeled verified metres. In context, the crossing monotonicity concerns positive fitted thresholds. S4 uses cellwise positive thresholds shared across directions and two fitted correlation parameters, not a universally shared two-parameter law.','Mainali2025 Fig4A-B; supplement S3/S4; parameter-crop image inspected')
ck('05c-place-tests.md',155,174,'Expectation is explicitly over independent zero-mean weights, so fixed input profiles need not have zero spatial means. The finite-dimensional central-limit condition includes normalization and no dominating term. Cross terms vanish in the covariance because weights are independent and centered.','Supplement S2 EqsS2-S4 and conditions afterS8; direct expectation algebra')
ck('05c-place-tests.md',175,200,'Dense uniform translated profiles give the covariance integral away from boundaries; independent weights do not themselves imply stationarity. Gaussian autocorrelation gives exp(-Delta²/(4b²)) and standard-deviation width sqrt2b. This width convention is explicitly stated. The final circuit conclusion remains a possible sufficient account and admits structured or learned alternatives.','Supplement S5-S8; direct completing square; Mainali2025 Discussion')
ck('06-synthesis.md',3,25,'The comparison distinguishes a spatial tuning function, a stored state coordinate and actual downstream eye motion. It keeps the 2022 upstream-source evidence and model sufficiency separate from an information-bound measurement and from the static2025 map. The table matches those objects.','2012 Eqs1-5;2022 Figs2-5;2025 Eq1; tbl:SYNTHESIS-MODELS')
ck('06-synthesis.md',29,52,'Composing fixed f_i with a moving x(t) is explicitly a guide construction. Taylor linearization and conditional variance2Dt give the covariance of expected-rate changes. Private spike noise, common fluctuations, finite movement and threshold corners are explicitly outside that formula.','Direct Taylor expansion and covariance identity; foundations tuning/covariance/diffusion teaching')
ck('06-synthesis.md',56,81,'With slopes2 and-1, displacement variance.01 gives rate variances.04,.01 and covariance-.02Hz². The one-source correlation is exactly-1 in the local linear example; independent private variance lowers its magnitude. The figure shows the correct+.1m displacement and paired changes, with no inhibitory-link inference.','Direct arithmetic and correlation formula; fig:SYNTHESIS-SHARED-POSITION inspected')
ck('06-synthesis.md',85,91,'The evidence comparison keeps fitted gain, finite-threshold model/data checks, calibration assumptions and the mathematical versus empirical status visible. Shared covariance is conditional on the decomposition assumptions, while stationary motor-noise amplitude alone cannot generate the modeled accumulating upstream component. A scaling exponent alone does not test the bound constant.','Mainali2025 STAR Methods; Ben-Shushan2022 Figs2-5/Methods; BurakFiete2012 Eqs1-5')
